# name|caveat shown by scripts/check-updates.sh when an update is available.
# Keep these generic (no company values). Add a row when you learn a downside the hard way.
neovim|Config (kickstart.nvim) and plugins can break on new minor releases; open nvim and run :checkhealth afterwards.
tree-sitter|Can change grammar/parser ABI; neovim treesitter parsers may need reinstalling (:TSUpdate). Release publishes no digest, so the hash is computed locally.
yazi|Config/plugin format changes between releases; `yazi` and `ya` must be updated together (both are linked from one archive).
resvg|Rendering output can change slightly; yazi SVG previews depend on it.
imagemagick|AppImage is extracted (about 100 MB+ per version); policy/format defaults can change between versions.
nerdctl|Must stay compatible with the containerd it talks to; check the container runtime version before upgrading.
talosctl|Keep within the supported version skew of your Talos clusters; upgrading ahead of the cluster can use newer API fields.
kubectl|Supported skew is one minor version either side of the cluster's API server; do not move ahead of your clusters blindly.
kubectl-minor|Moves the pinned Kubernetes apt repo to a new minor; check cluster version skew first. Needs apt-repos.sh edit (K8S_MINOR) and a sudo rerun; the Kubernetes key fingerprint is not pinned.
terraform|State files and provider locks can be upgraded irreversibly by a newer Terraform; teammates on older versions may then be unable to use the state. Check required_version constraints.
vault|CLI/server version skew can matter; check the server version you talk to before upgrading.
golang-go|Toolchain change affects builds; go.mod `toolchain`/`go` lines may trigger downloads of other versions.
ffmpeg|Large dependency set; yazi video previews rely on it.
